  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "First where are we going wrong?",
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 1.959
    },
    {
      "text": "We need housing in the cities, where the people and the jobs are.",
      "start": 4.179,
      "end": 7.299
    },
    {
      "text": "Instead we build outward, paving over farmland at the edge of town sealing soil that rain can't drain through, wiring in a car commute for everyone who moves there.",
      "start": 7.619,
      "end": 16.26
    },
    {
      "text": "Germany's own target is under THIRTY hectares of new land a day by 2030.",
      "start": 17.5,
      "end": 21.459
    },
    {
      "text": "We're sitting at FIFTY.",
      "start": 21.76,
      "end": 22.719
    },
    {
      "text": "So much for the target.",
      "start": 24.019,
      "end": 25.039
    },
    {
      "text": "Meanwhile, there's an obvious place to put those homes, and we're standing on it: the roofs we already have.",
      "start": 25.68,
      "end": 30.659
    },
    {
      "text": "The studies reckon about one point one MILLION apartments could go on top of existing housing blocks alone up to one and a half million if you add offices, supermarkets, parking decks.",
      "start": 31.26,
      "end": 40.559
    },
    {
      "text": "No new land, right where it's needed.",
      "start": 41.579,
      "end": 43.299
    },
    {
      "text": "That's Aufstockung building on top of what's already there.",
      "start": 43.599,
      "end": 46.459
    },
    {
      "text": "So why does almost none of it happen?",
      "start": 47.0,
      "end": 48.539
    },
    {
      "text": "The usual suspects height limits, parking rules, owners who can't agree.",
      "start": 49.579,
      "end": 53.579
    },
    {
      "text": "But mostly because actually pulling it off is harder than it looks.",
      "start": 54.139,
      "end": 57.059
    }
  ]
